<speak>I've got the page here, but my handwriting is not helping me today. Let me read from my notes: my <sub alias="eff eye en">FIN</sub> is <sub alias="gee">G</sub> nine two four five four three one <sub alias="ex">X</sub>. Sorry, I misread my handwriting; my correct <sub alias="eff eye en">FIN</sub> is <sub alias="gee">G</sub> nine two four seven four three one <sub alias="ex">X</sub>. My date of birth is the twenty-fourth of April nineteen eighty-one. That's why I prefer keeping the original document beside my notebook. When I copy things quickly at the office, everything looks obvious at the time, then a week later I can't tell what I meant. My wife keeps telling me to stop squeezing notes into the margins, and I think she has a fair point.</speak>